n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}$ is an even function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}$ is an even function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115257/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2688742c-1655-557a-888d-af7e2179a89c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88587/selection/ad5f4205204102e8d69d265f70178933cf857a0601b98a7c97f6bd4c0351b975" :answer/id #uuid "299ed189-3300-5f59-94fb-ad1d5dc7ef8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{10}(-2{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88587/selection/de914812f1869b0d6a828809cb8bb851fdd531a0bc65390e8d1cf465bc4ae123" :answer/id #uuid "0bc37c4c-d092-503e-bda6-73312fdb7ff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{5}(-2{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88587/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "20638ad6-be59-5770-b0ec-3e69d838e62a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88587/selection/f0b36f187e8f6c8add65e4b2984a4b7fb17c2865d508f138f413c5f2f5fcfcb8" :answer/id #uuid "6fcc9bec-27d7-5e19-9872-d691b1111c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{\\int }_{0}^{5}(-2{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88587/selection/02a0395894f58c3431f8d311bb21a062007141e19ec25e7e89419d15a46bcc1d" :answer/id #uuid "c8f07549-922f-510c-956d-b106605701ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{5}(-2{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88587/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d729cec-b194-5edf-96ac-5799f46cdd08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88587/selection/02a0395894f58c3431f8d311bb21a062007141e19ec25e7e89419d15a46bcc1d" :answer-field/choices ["q-88587/selection/ad5f4205204102e8d69d265f70178933cf857a0601b98a7c97f6bd4c0351b975" "q-88587/selection/de914812f1869b0d6a828809cb8bb851fdd531a0bc65390e8d1cf465bc4ae123" "q-88587/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-88587/selection/f0b36f187e8f6c8add65e4b2984a4b7fb17c2865d508f138f413c5f2f5fcfcb8" "q-88587/selection/02a0395894f58c3431f8d311bb21a062007141e19ec25e7e89419d15a46bcc1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88587" :question/id #uuid "08d1c857-ad7f-54d3-8cc2-8674402a4da7" :question/math-academy-id "q-88587" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-5}^{5}(-2{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any even function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ is symmetric across the $y$-axis, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=-2{x}^{4}$ is an even function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =-2(-x)^{4} \\\\  & =-2{x}^{4} \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=-2{x}^{4}$ is an even function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}(-2{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{5}(-2{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-88587/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2688742c-1655-557a-888d-af7e2179a89c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88587"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115255/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892