t{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to zero due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x){e}^{-(-x)^{2}} \\\\  & =-x{e}^{-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-7}^{7}x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{x}$  is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)^{2}{e}^{(-x)} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{e}^{-x} \\\\  & \\ne -g(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)=(x+1)^{3}$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =((-x)+1)^{3} \\\\  & =(1-x)^{3} \\\\  & \\ne -h(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88695/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-156183/selection/c3a62c99faba2ab07d5426a7ec7c130855c517c33a16b838458b1f46d671e0f5" :answer/id #uuid "d10889e2-126c-56ff-af17-666e924e98c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({2}^{x}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{x}})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156183/selection/57afceef7e41eb3dcd12bcd35e0719ecb59f2f32713db9237c276e28800d3366" :answer/id #uuid "882e2bc8-40aa-59b2-a10d-6237dabc4fc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({2}^{x}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{x}})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156183/selection/05d181dda44bb18414d9bd65eba2fdb82ddd55cd1c81973e806ccd4a8cd52735" :answer/id #uuid "5cac3ee0-abf1-511b-8656-df6c4de0e4d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{\\int }_{0}^{2}({2}^{x}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{x}})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id